Installation
------------

To install, just run:

 make

followed by:

 make install

as root. You can set DESTDIR to change the installation target:

 make install DESTDIR=/my/custom/installation/target

You can set the CPU arch with an ARCH variable. It sets the compiler
flags used by make, and whether make install sets up depfinder for
lib64 directories (x86_64 and aarch64), so give it to both:

 make ARCH=i586
 make install ARCH=i586

The default value is ARCH=x86_64. CXXFLAGS and LDFLAGS from the
environment are used instead of the default compiler flags for ARCH,
if they are set.

To run the test suite (it doesn't need depfinder to be installed):

 make check


Uninstallation
--------------
To remove, you can just:

 rm /usr/bin/depfinder
 rm /usr/libexec/depfinder-search
 rm /usr/libexec/depfinder-python
 rm /usr/man/man1/depfinder.1
